    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "COMPUTE",
      "narration_text": "Compute first. Pruning, quantization, and distillation can shrink a model dramatically, so the revision makes compression the default path to field deployment. But that evidence comes from general deep learning, not SERS. The paper found no published result showing a compressed SERS model holding its accuracy under real substrate and hot-spot variability. So treat compression as a step with an expected cost.",
