    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "INTERPRET",
      "narration_text": "Interpretability got a real update. The draft called mechanistic explanation an open problem. Since then, dedicated methods have appeared. Zaki and colleagues built CRIME, an explanation method designed for SERS mixtures. Yang and colleagues' GRASS groups a Raman spectrum into regions before scoring them, instead of scoring every wavenumber on its own. The recommendation: reach for a spectral method, not unmodified GradCAM.",
