    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "GENERALIZE",
      "narration_text": "Generalization is the hardest. Models trained at one site, on one instrument and one substrate batch, often fail when any of those change. The revision called this untouched territory, but there's early SERS work now. Mahmud and colleagues translated spectra from four portable instruments into lab-grade equivalents. That covers devices on one substrate type. Cross-site and cross-substrate generalization are still open.",
